Explanation of the change:

1. **Problem**  
   In 1.20.x, `preHandleData` was doing
   ```js
   item.pos = pos;
   item.level = level;
   // …
   k2n[key] = p2n[pos] = { …item };
   ```
   When your `dataSource` items come from an immutable/frozen structure, `item.pos = pos` will throw, or silently fail, leading to missing entries in `k2n`/`p2n` and finally a `getNodeProps(…)` lookup of `undefined`.

2. **Solution**  
   We first shallow-clone each `item` into `newItem = { ...item }`, then assign all calculated fields (`pos`, `level`, `key`, `isLeaf`, `isLastChild` and the cloned `children`).  Because `newItem` is a fresh object, assigning new properties is perfectly safe.  Finally we write `k2n[key] = p2n[pos] = newItem` and return `newItem`.  This guarantees that every node in the map is defined, and no mutation of your frozen original data ever happens.

With this one change all positions will be correctly generated and stored, and your downstream `getNodeProps` lookups will never see an undefined entry again.
